# Tenant isolation and auth

Every organization-owned query must include `organizationId` from the authenticated session.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
prisma.project.findUnique({ where: { id: projectId } })

// ✅ GOOD
prisma.project.findFirst({
  where: { id: projectId, organizationId: ctx.organizationId },
})
```

Check permissions on the server (not role name alone). Never trust the frontend. Do not expose secrets, passwords, tokens, or payment credentials in logs, GraphQL, or audit payloads.

Critical workflows (lead conversion, proposal accept, bid accept, payment updates) must use Prisma transactions. BidRequest allows only one winning bid — enforce with constraints + transactions, not UI locking.

Clients must not see bidding internals, freelancer costs, or profit. Freelancers must not see other private bids or agency margin.
